-- Seed data ported from the MySQL dump.
-- MySQL backslash escapes were converted to SQLite doubled quotes
-- (e.g. DON\'T -> DON''T, Ahmad \'Izzuddin -> Ahmad ''Izzuddin).
-- Insert order matters: users first, then events/items (SQLite enforces FKs).

-- Every demo account shares the password "unifind123". The hash below is scrypt
-- (see lib/auth.ts for the format); the salt is fixed so the seed stays
-- byte-for-byte reproducible.
--
-- user_id is written out for the same reason events.event_id is: a profile
-- picture's id is built from it ("P101" is user 1's picture, see
-- lib/imageId.ts), so an id that moved with the list order would quietly hand
-- somebody else's face to an account. The order below is created_at order,
-- which is what the live database's ids already are. The first eighteen
-- accounts ship with the demo picture public/img/pfp/P<user_id>01.jpeg; the
-- rest keep the initial-letter avatar.



-- A seeded record's pictures are contiguous from …01, so its lifetime counter is
-- simply how many pictures its array holds. That is what makes the next picture
-- it ever creates the following number — an id is never handed out twice (see
-- lib/imageId.ts), so removing one from a live record does not free its number
-- for the next upload.
UPDATE events SET image_seq = json_array_length(images) WHERE images IS NOT NULL;
UPDATE items  SET image_seq = json_array_length(images) WHERE images IS NOT NULL;
